urname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Hogg</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Knox</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Acute admissions to medical beds</article-title><source>Journal of the Royal College of General Practitioners</source><year>1972</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>211</fpage><lpage>219</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">5074428</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Glasby</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Littlechild</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Pryce</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Show me the way to go home: delayed hospital discharged and older people</article-title><source>Health Services Management Centre and Institute for Applied Social Sciences, University of Birmingham</source><year>2004</year><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.hsmc.bham.ac.uk/research/pdfs/HospDischfinalrep.pdf"/></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hermans</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Anten</surname><given-names>HW</given-names></name><name><surname>Diederiks</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Philipsen</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Beeren</surname><given-names>HW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Patient characteristics with predictive significance for 'blocked bed' problems in the neurological department of a general hospital</article-title><source>Ned Tijdschr Geneeskd</source><year>1995</year><volume>139</volume><fpage>890</fpage><lpage>894</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7739738</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mayo</surname><given-names>NE</given-names></name><name><surname>Wood-Dauphinee</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Gayton</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Scott</surname><given-names>SC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Nonmedical bed-days for stroke patients admitted to acute-care hospitals in Montreal, Canada</article-title><source>Stroke</source><year>1997</year><volume>28</volume><fpage>543</fpage><lpage>549</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9056609</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Playford</surname><given-names>ED</given-names></name><name><surname>Crawford</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Monro</surname><given-names>PS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A survey of neurological disability at a district general hospital</article-title><source>The British Journal of Clinical Practice</source><year>1994</year><volume>48</volume><fpage>304</fpage><lpage>306</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7848792</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>van Straten</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Meulen</surname><given-names>JH van der</given-names></name><name><surname>Bos</surname><given-names>GA van den</given-names></name><name><surname>Limburg</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Length of hospital stay and discharge delays in stroke patients</article-title><source>Stroke</source><year>1997</year><volume>28</volume><fpage>137</fpage><lpage>140</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8996502</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schluep</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Bogousslavsky</surname><given-names>J</given-names><